---
description: Use a vision model to verify that UI changes visually enhance the website
alwaysApply: false
---
Before making any code or content changes, capture baseline screenshots for all breakpoints.

```bash
bun visual_qa/capture_anchors.mjs \
  --base-url http://localhost:4321 \
  --start-dev \
  --label baseline \
  "#home" "#about" "#projects" "#writing" "#events"
```

After making changes, capture candidate screenshots:

```bash
bun visual_qa/capture_anchors.mjs \
  --base-url http://localhost:4321 \
    --start-dev \
    --label candidate \
  "#home" "#about" "#projects" "#writing" "#events"
```

The script will automatically compare candidate screenshots against baseline and report changes.

Review images that show differences. Flag both functional and aesthetic visual regressions. Consider, for example,

1. **Color cohesion & contrast**
2. **Text readability**
3. **Layout & spacing**
4. **Responsiveness / hierarchy preservation**
5. **Cohesion & wow factor**

Once you are satisfied, it is recommended to seek a second opinion from Google Gemini. If a GEMINI_API_KEY is available in either .env or as an environment variable, you may use it to call the latest Gemini Flash model with the SDK or command-line tool of your choice.